.TH HEE-GOOSE 1 "2026-09-13" "HEE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hee-goose \- honk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hee goose
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints
.B HONK
in italics and a goose. That is all it does.
.PP
The goose is rendered with
.BR chafa (1),
which uses the kitty graphics protocol where the terminal supports it. Set
.B HEE_GOOSE_IMAGE
to render another image.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ hee goose
\fIHONK\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
followed by the goose, drawn in the terminal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HEE_GOOSE_IMAGE
Path to the image chafa renders instead of the shipped goose.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chafa (1)
